@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g2-validity`
IMPORT `g2-second-schedule`
IMPORT `g2-conditions`
IMPORT `g2-temporary-licence`
IMPORT `g2-renewal`
IMPORT `g2-tests-fixtures`

-- g2-tests-red.l4: expectations that are MEANT TO FAIL.
-- Each assertion below states, as if it were the answer, the result of a reading that this group considered and did NOT take
-- (the forks of FRAGMENT-G2.md section 2): it must fail while the encoding takes the other reading.  The same alternative
-- readings are asserted TO HOLD, through their own callable functions, in the other g2-tests- modules.  This file is the proof
-- that the harness can fail, and each failure here is expected: the number of assertions in this file is the number of failures
-- check.sh must report for it (44: 33 from the first delivery, less the two FC2 and FC7 lines that hold since the D1 repair of 2026-10-14, plus eight old
-- green assertions moved here by it, plus five new ones for FC2 and FS11).  Nothing here is a finding about the Law.

GIVETH A Licence
`a licence granted on 1.2.2026 and renewed on 15.6.2030` MEANS
    `a licence of kind` `grade 1 licence` `, temporary being` FALSE `, granted on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `, renewed on` (LIST (YMD 2030 6 15)) `, recorded to end` NOTHING `, revoked` NOTHING `, suspended from` NOTHING `, suspended until` NOTHING

GIVETH A Licence
`a licence granted on 1.2.2026 whose register records 30.4.2031` MEANS
    `a licence of kind` `grade 1 licence` `, temporary being` FALSE `, granted on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `, renewed on` EMPTY `, recorded to end` (JUST (YMD 2031 4 30)) `, revoked` NOTHING `, suspended from` NOTHING `, suspended until` NOTHING

GIVETH A Licence
`a licence granted on 1.2.2026 and revoked on 1.5.2028` MEANS
    `a licence of kind` `grade 1 licence` `, temporary being` FALSE `, granted on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `, renewed on` EMPTY `, recorded to end` NOTHING `, revoked` (JUST (YMD 2028 5 1)) `, suspended from` NOTHING `, suspended until` NOTHING

GIVEN reading IS A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
      kind IS A `Licence kind`
      applicant IS AN Applicant
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the item numbers under` reading `for a` kind `by` applicant `made on` day MEANS
    map (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number`)
        (`Second Schedule — the items that apply under` reading `to` (`an application for a` kind `by` applicant `made on` day) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests`)

GIVEN kind IS A `Licence kind`
      applicant IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the item numbers for a` kind `by` applicant MEANS
    `the item numbers under` `the reading of the Second Schedule taken` `for a` kind `by` applicant `made on` `the usual application day`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Period of work on cooling systems`
`365 days of work to 31.8.2026` MEANS LIST `a period of work from` (YMD 2025 9 1) `to` (YMD 2026 8 31)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Period of work on cooling systems`
`work from 2.9.2025 to the application day 1.9.2026` MEANS LIST `a period of work from` (YMD 2025 9 2) `to` (YMD 2026 9 1)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Period of work on cooling systems`
`two overlapping periods of work in the year to 30.6.2026` MEANS LIST (`a period of work from` (YMD 2025 9 1) `to` (YMD 2026 6 30)), (`a period of work from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 6 30))
GIVETH A LIST OF `Period of work on cooling systems`
`work from 2.7.2025 to 30.6.2028` MEANS LIST `a period of work from` (YMD 2025 7 2) `to` (YMD 2028 6 30)

§ `Red — section 8`

-- FV1 (T24): the year of grant counted as the first year would make the last day 31.3.2030; the reading taken makes it 1.2.2031.
#ASSERT `s 8 — the last day of the validity period beginning on` (YMD 2026 2 1) EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31
-- FV2: Interpretation Law s 10(c) applied to the five year limb (Saturday and Sunday rest) would move 1.2.2031 to 3.2.2031; not applied in the reading taken.
#ASSERT `s 8 — the last day of the validity period beginning on` (YMD 2026 2 1) EQUALS YMD 2031 2 3
-- FV3: each further period continuing from the end of the previous would make the last day 2.2.2036; the reading taken gives 31.3.2035.
#ASSERT `s 8 — the last day of validity of the licence` `a licence granted on 1.2.2026 and renewed on 15.6.2030` EQUALS YMD 2036 2 2
-- FV4: validity beginning the day after the grant would make the licence not in force on the grant day; the reading taken has it in force.
#ASSERT NOT `the licence is in force on` (`an ordinary grade 1 licence granted on` (YMD 2026 2 1)) (YMD 2026 2 1)
-- FV5: the Law alone, ignoring the register's recorded last day, would give 1.2.2031; the reading taken lets the register govern (30.4.2031).
#ASSERT `s 8 — the last day of validity of the licence` `a licence granted on 1.2.2026 whose register records 30.4.2031` EQUALS YMD 2031 2 1
-- FV6: a revocation taking effect the day after the day recorded would leave the licence in force on 1.5.2028; the reading taken does not.
#ASSERT `the licence is in force on` `a licence granted on 1.2.2026 and revoked on 1.5.2028` (YMD 2028 5 1)
-- FV7 (T25): an extension capped at the 31 March limb would end 31.3.2031; the reading taken lets it run to 1.5.2031.
#ASSERT `s 17(c) — the last day of validity` (YMD 2031 2 1) `extended by` 3 `months` EQUALS YMD 2031 3 31

§ `Red — the Second Schedule`

-- FS1 (T1): the ungraded certificate row reaching every grade would put the grade 1 certificate holder in B3 and B5 (Part B) and C3 and C6 (Part C).
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)) EQUALS LIST 3, 5
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)) EQUALS LIST 4, 6
-- FS2 (T2): item 1 only for an applicant with no prior training at all would leave the 3-unit holder in no item of Part A.
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 3 study units`)) EQUALS EMPTY
-- FS2 (T2): B1(2) reached by the 5-unit holder would put B1 and B5 together; B1 alone would be "the certificate itself suffices".
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 5 study units`)) EQUALS LIST 1, 5
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 5 study units`)) EQUALS LIST 1
-- FS3 (T3): registration alone reaching every registered applicant would put the technician with the programme in B2 and B6, the practical engineer with it in C2 and C7.
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant registered as a technician, programme completed being` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST 2, 6
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant registered as a practical engineer, programme completed being` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST 2, 7
-- FS9: a lapsed licence (granted 1.1.2018, ended 1.1.2023) counting as "a grade 1 licence" would put its holder in B3.
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only the licences` (LIST (`an ordinary grade 1 licence granted on` (YMD 2018 1 1)))) EQUALS LIST 3
-- FS5 (T6): reading "up to N" as exactly N would give the hours the applicant must complete; the reading taken refuses to say.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Second Schedule (up to N read as exactly N) — the hours the applicant must complete under` (`training of up to` 350 `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)
-- FS6 (T4): the wiki's layout of Part C item 4, with an empty column B, as the answer; the gazette's column B has 240 hours.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Second Schedule — the requirements in column B of` (LIST `Second Schedule, Part C, item 4`)
-- FS7: a year of experience as 366 days would put the 365-day applicant in item 1, not A2; adding overlapping periods or counting the application day would put the others in A2.
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant with only the periods of work` `365 days of work to 31.8.2026`) EQUALS LIST 1
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant with only the periods of work` `work from 2.9.2025 to the application day 1.9.2026`) EQUALS LIST 2
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant with only the periods of work` `two overlapping periods of work in the year to 30.6.2026`) EQUALS LIST 2
-- FS8: Interpretation Law s 10(c) applied to the three-year note would move 16.7.2028 (a Sunday) to 17.7.2028.
#ASSERT `Second Schedule column C — the last day of the three years beginning on` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS YMD 2028 7 17
-- FS8: the note tested on the day of decision (1.8.2028) would close the experience item for an application made on 1.7.2028.
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant with only the periods of work` `work from 2.7.2025 to 30.6.2028`) EQUALS LIST 1
-- FS8 (T7): the anchor of s 63(a)(2) (16.1.2027) would keep the experience items open on 1.1.2029; the anchor of s 63(a)(1) does not.
#ASSERT `Second Schedule column C — the experience items are in force on the day` (YMD 2025 7 16) (YMD 2029 1 1)

§ `Red — section 6`

-- FC1: s 6(a) read without regulation 4 would make the Registrar bound to grant though the fee was not paid.
#ASSERT `the Registrar must grant the licence` (`an application on the usual day for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` `an applicant with nothing`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- FC3: the programme's approval not being a condition would let completion in an unapproved programme qualify.
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` `an applicant with nothing` `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
-- FC4: the youth school certificate not counting as a final certificate.
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a)(4)(a) — the applicant holds a final certificate` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a certificate of the Training Division vocational school for youth`)))

§ `Red — section 9`

-- FT1: s 6(a)(1) and (3) still asked of the foreign expert would fail the non-adult expert; the reading taken does not ask them.
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(a) — the applicant is a foreign expert meeting conditions (1) to (3)` (`a foreign expert whose applicant is` (`an applicant who is adult` FALSE `, citizen` FALSE `, resident` FALSE `, with the record` `a clean record`)) TRUE
-- FT2: Interpretation Law s 10(c) applied to the one-year cap would move 1.2.2027 (a Monday, if a rest day) to 2.2.2027.
#ASSERT `s 9(a) — the latest last day of a temporary licence granted on` (YMD 2026 2 1) EQUALS YMD 2027 2 2
-- FT3: the renewal's cap counted from the day of a renewal on 15.3.2027 would be 15.3.2028; counted from the end of the term renewed (31.1.2027) it is 31.1.2028.
#ASSERT `s 9(b) — the latest last day of a term renewing one that ended on` (YMD 2027 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2028 3 15
-- FT4: work on the application day itself counting as "before" it.
#ASSERT `s 9(a)(2) — the expert is authorised abroad and did similar work in the six preceding years` (`an expert qualifying in all but the work, which is` (LIST (`a piece of work abroad on` (YMD 2026 9 1) `, similar being` TRUE)))
-- FT5: "above 70 kW" read as "at least 70 kW".
#ASSERT `s 9(a)(1) — the expert was invited to work on a system above 70 kW` (`an expert qualifying in all but the capacity of the system, which is` 70)

§ `Red — the Division certificate of the grade sought (forks FS10 and FS11, defect D1 of 2026-10-14)`

-- Before the repair the module took the literal reading of FS10: the Division certificate of the grade sought was a column A entry of the ungraded row, and its
-- holder was asked for up to 50, 50 or 200 hours more.  The eight assertions below are the old green assertions, MOVED here unchanged: they state the literal
-- reading as if it were the answer, and now fail on the reading taken.  The same readings hold through their own functions (`the reading with the Division
-- certificate of the grade sought as an ordinary column A entry (FS10)`, `s 6(a) under the reading`) in g2-tests-second-schedule.l4 and g2-tests-conditions.l4.
-- FS10 literal: the grade 2 holder asked for B5(1)
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
-- FS10 literal: the grade 1 holder asked for A3
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
-- FS10 literal: the grade 3 holder in C6
#ASSERT map (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number`) (`training required for the licence sought` (`an application for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `the commencement day in the tests`) EQUALS LIST 6
-- FS10 literal: the grade 3 holder asked for C6
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
-- FS10 literal: the grade 2 holder asked for B5(1)
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
-- FS10 literal: the grade 1 holder in A3
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)) EQUALS LIST 3
-- FS10 literal: the grade 2 holder in B5(1)
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)) EQUALS LIST 5
-- FS10 literal: the grade 3 holder in C6
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) EQUALS LIST 6
-- FC2 (its discriminating applicant since D1): "in accordance with the Second Schedule" asking nothing further would qualify the registered technician with the programme
-- by limb (b) alone for a grade 1 licence; Part A has no item for registrants, so the default item asks for 350 hours or a 3-unit certificate.
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant registered as a technician, programme completed being` TRUE TRUE) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
-- FS11: a certificate of a higher grade meeting item 1 would put a grade 3 certificate holder seeking grade 1 or 2, and a grade 2 holder seeking grade 1, in item 1 alone;
-- the reading taken leaves them in the ungraded row (A3, B5(1)).
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) EQUALS LIST 1
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) EQUALS LIST 1
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)) EQUALS LIST 1
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
